    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30730" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕocles</span></b> , is and i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νεοκλῆς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The father of Themistocles</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Them.
				1, 1 sq.</span></i>—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕōclīdes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>the descendant of
				Neocles</i>, i. e. <i>Themistocles</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 1,
				3, 69</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The father of Epicurus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				1, 26, 72</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A painter</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				11, 40, § 146</span></i>.</div>
